":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T04:43:07-08:00","id":1176923,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, the Toothcracker entry is just inspired by some of my own neuroses/nightmares. Well, the bit with the building pressure cracking the teeth is - the rest is all just spun out of that initial base concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T05:07:20-08:00","id":1176927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1176040-five-pounds-of-meat?p=1176923#post1176923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what it's worth, the Toothcracker entry is just inspired by some of my own neuroses/nightmares. Well, the bit with the building pressure cracking the teeth is - the rest is all just spun out of that initial base concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>That elevates your writing to art.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T05:38:37-08:00","id":1176930,"title":"","content":"Huh. I was thinking the infection and the Toothwights were some creation of a Rank 6+ spirit of Teeth, Anxiety and the Occult at first, but the real answer is even weirder.<br /> <br /> Is there a reason she has no merits though? Or are her powers structured as merits?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T05:40:18-08:00","id":1176931,"title":"","content":"I feel the need to share this, both as a curiousity and for worldbuilding:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.bbc.com/future/story/20160301-the-gruesome-and-mysterious-case-of-exploding-teeth\" target=\"_blank\">The gruesome and mysterious case of exploding teeth.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T07:37:03-08:00","id":1176946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1176040-five-pounds-of-meat?p=1176930#post1176930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. I was thinking the infection and the Toothwights were some creation of a Rank 6+ spirit of Teeth, Anxiety and the Occult at first, but the real answer is even weirder.<br /> <br /> Is there a reason she has no merits though? Or are her powers structured as merits?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b'cos I forgot merits. That said I can't really think of any interesting ones to add to her that aren't basically just very minor in impact compared to her main suite of powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1176040-five-pounds-of-meat?p=1176931#post1176931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel the need to share this, both as a curiousity and for worldbuilding:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.bbc.com/future/story/20160301-the-gruesome-and-mysterious-case-of-exploding-teeth\" target=\"_blank\">The gruesome and mysterious case of exploding teeth.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat's amazing. Guess I now know when the tooth harvester first became active <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200bOn a side-note: Gonna be a while before I get to the next entry in this thread. I have a tabletop game tonight, then I'm heading off on Friday afternoon for a weekend-long plot management meeting for a big UK larp that I'm on the plot team for. As such, I likely won't even have time to consider writing the next one up til Monday. So don't worry if you don't see anything new from me in this thread for a while - I haven't forgotten about it, and I'm not burned out (yet)!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T08:50:03-08:00","id":1176961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1176040-five-pounds-of-meat?p=1176842#post1176842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Time to make some STL models. Does that count as one or two of five?</div> </div> </div> </div>What's an STL model?<br /> <br /> \u200bThis entry counts as one; that there's two stat blocks doesn't change that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T10:06:55-08:00","id":1176997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1176040-five-pounds-of-meat?p=1176961#post1176961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What's an STL model?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be something like <a href=\"https://www.thingiverse.com/thing:2761507\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>. They are digital models that can then be loaded into a 3D printer. I have a thread of CofD related stuff I've made in the main Chronicles forum. A good chunk of them are of Werewolf stuff. <br /> <br /> I don't usually do scenery, I'm more focused on monster minis, but the idea of a tooth-based plant was too neat (and creepy) to pass up. I do have some other ideas, but it may take some time, so I'll link to them as they get made. This entry had made me really happy that you're also writing for Deviant. And now that I think about it, a Toothcracker that somehow retained their personality and is now trying to avoid/strike back at the Maiden of the Maw would be an awesome Deviant!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T18:52:47-08:00","id":1177123,"title":"","content":"A particularly powerful drop of nightmare fuel you've written, here. I can see much here that could leave a certain pack, and their players, disgusted with the Maiden of the Maw, hopefully they never have to face her. <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Seth would totally mistake a Toothwight for some kind of tooth-spirit claimed, if they did.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":2598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","user":"Gryphon's Feather","date":". 01-18-2018, 10:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T20:05:06-08:00","id":1177143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1176040-five-pounds-of-meat?p=1176797#post1176797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>\u200bToothcracker</b></span><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Reminded me of Qian Ya from Shadowrun, Hong Kong.<br /> <br /> She's a Yama King (the Queen With a Thousand Teeth). She creates demons made out of enamel and gum tissue!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-18-2018, 11:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T23:57:03-08:00","id":1177191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1176040-five-pounds-of-meat?p=1177143#post1177143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Reminded me of Qian Ya from Shadowrun, Hong Kong.<br /> <br /> She's a Yama King (the Queen With a Thousand Teeth). She creates demons made out of enamel and gum tissue!</div> </div> </div> </div>And she could give you 7 years of extremely good luck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T02:31:52-08:00","id":1177210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1176040-five-pounds-of-meat?p=1177191#post1177191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And she could give you 7 years of extremely good luck.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I thought that was funny, because the story mode for the DLC expansion plays out differently if you make a deal with her. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T20:42:31-08:00","id":1177508,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.thingiverse.com/thing:2763169\" target=\"_blank\">Here's another tooth tree!</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T07:35:45-08:00","id":1178782,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>MEATWAVE</b></span><br /> It pours through the airwaves, a broth that seeps in through the eyes and ears and simmers in the brain. It's a putrescence chewing pixels out of an advert for HIGH PROTEIN SUPPLEMENTS and THE LATEST DIET TREND! It's a sour note flitting amongst the chords of the chart-topping pop song, a hidden bass whenever the starlet screams about heat and bodies and sweat. It's a new way of living, the impossibly-white teeth of a smiling presenter, a blood-slick butcher's board, concerned voices on the radio talking about how to feed the population, the pulsing lights of a promise of exotic and distant travels where the people are different and surely more primal, more alive, more real than the hollowed-out, empty, tasteless existence you're drowning. It's meatwave <b>Meatwave MEATWAVE</b>.<br /> <br /> MEATWAVE is a multi-part process of monstrosity, a corporate body concerned with flesh and bone - spiritual technology, or technological spirituality, that overturns the simple constancy of meat and sinew in favour of something new and hungry. MEATWAVE isn't about the same old same old, the humdrum, the boring days where each has the same dull stasis with your innards on the inside and your skin a cold, isolating barrier from the fleshy unity of the rest of life. MEATWAVE is fresh. MEATWAVE is the future. MEATWAVE Is what you want to be, and how you want to be.<br /> <br /> The initial vectors of MEATWAVE are data spirits - entities of radio and light and information. They do a lot of the drudge work of the enterprise; they sink their claws into the pulpy brain matter of the humans who need to serve as the infection nodes. The spirit goes after its chosen target directly - an anchorman, a singer, a media executive - and attacks through something the human reads or hears, beginning the process of turning them Ridden and eventually Claimed. The Claimed serves as the hub for the support network that needs to grow - the humans caught in its orbit who give it further access to media outputs. This forms a cell or cult dedicated to pushing MEATWAVE out onto the data highway and into the population.<br /> <br /> So far, so normal, inasmuch as Claimed tend to behave; but it's MEATWAVE that makes this different. There's something wrong with the hive of radio spirits tangled up in this affair, even by the frankly gutchurning proclivities that such spirits tend towards normally when given a chance to meddle in the Flesh. They're a little bit magath round the edges - a little bit meat, a little bit gristle, not enough to drive them deranged but enough to mark them as servants of the MEATWAVE. Their Claimed forms soon turn nauseating, forcing a retirement from public activity and greater influence through human cultists instead. The main thing is, though, that they know the secret codes of the MEATWAVE - a rite, a manipulation of the laws of Flesh and Shadow being wrought on a massive scale. They aren't the originators - they're just the heralds.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>MEATWAVE-Claimed</b></span><br /> Int 5 Wits 4 Res 3 Str 5 Dex 2 Sta 5 Pre 6 Man 6 Com 3<br /> Academics 2 Computer 3 Crafts 4 Occult 3 Politics 2 Athletics 3 Brawl 2 Drive 2 Larceny 1 Stealth 2 Weaponry 3 Empathy 4 Expression 5 Intimidation 3 Persuasion 4 Socialize 4 Subterfuge 5<br /> Merits: Allies (Variers) 4, Contacts 3 (Varies), Fame 1, Fast-Talking 5, Resources 4, Status (Varies) 3<br /> Willpower 6 Essence 15 Health 10 Initiative 5 Defence 5 Speed 12<br /> <b>Influences:</b> Data 2 Flesh 1<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Eye Spy, Gauntlet Cloak, Hunter's Senses (MEATWAVE-affected humans), Hypnotic Gaze, Interface, Natural Weapons 2, Pierce MInd<br /> <b>Flesh Transmitter:</b> After incapacitating a human with its natural weapons, the Claimed can spend 3 Essence to transform the victim over the course of an hour. This rebuilds the human into a twisted amalgam of technical machinery, meat, and bone - a living transmitter, flesh pierced by vanes and antennae, innards threaded with wires and optics. A transmitter allows the Claimed to use Hypnotic Gaze and Pierce Mind against all humans within a mile who are seeing or listening to a media device such as a TV, radio, etc. Adding more flesh transmitters to a comingled gestalt increases the range by another mile, up to a maximum of fourty-four miles. A human transformed into a transmitter cannot be reverted back to their original form and is essentially incapable of doing anything other than occasionally twitch or moan to express their agony.<br /> <b>Cartilage Panoply:</b> By touching a MEATWAVE-affected human or cultist and spending 1 Essence, the Claimed can cause the target's body to buckle, twist and reshape instantly into battle-panoply for the Claimed. Spine and ribs crack and reshape into a shield, guts hanging loosely below them as limbs flop off and the head blossoms into a cranial plate; or the human arches forwards, arms coming together and melding into a cruel sickle-shaped blade of resculpted bone and sinew as the useless lower body comes apart in a welter of blood and meat-parts; or the human is dragged into an embrace, innards pulping as the skin and meat slides across the Claimed's torso to form a pulsating gambeson. A human reshaped in this way either increases the natural weapons of the Claimed by effectively raising it to 4 dots (yes, this does go above the usual maximum of 3), gives the Claimed 3 points of armour, or provides the Claimed with 1 more point of armour and an additional point of Defence. Each option can be used in subsequent turns if the Claimed has more suitable humans on-hand, but a given option can't be used more than once in a scene. The humans are obviously tragically reforged in the process and there is no way to reverse it; they will die at the end of the scene and their remains are useless, requiring new targets if the Claimed wants to use this Dread Power in the future.<br /> <br /> Now, the MEATWAVE idea-virus that manifests itself in the bubbling data of the media stream doesn't necessarily have immediate or drastic effects. Sometimes it latches on to the brain of a human and just simmers there, pushing gently like the weakest of Ridden. Eat more meat, it says, or, change your life. Seek out the things that thrill you, it mutters. Indulge your appetites - all of them. It gives gentle dreams of gnashing teeth and flesh against flesh. It occasionally spikes into skinless nightmares of unity-of-meat, of cathedrals of sinew and intestines. Travel, it says. Consume. Meet new people and crack their skulls open with a rock and eat the spattered brain-matter. Run across the plains and hunt and revel. Break the mould. Live free. Eat<b> eat EAT</b>.<br /> <br /> Disquieting, even disgusting, but such a call-of-the-void is sufficiently low-key that it won't do a great deal to most humans it touches. They're infected, but they're probably just upset by the experience. It adds another layer to the deviant voices in the back of the head urging them to do things society tells them they should not, but humans are remarkably good at pretending those urges aren't there. A few decide to change their lives and start on new fad diets (meat meat MEAT but a surprising number turn vegan) or go travelling or start taking drugs. A few break, suffering episodes of irrationality or violence, and the police who turn up at the apartment take a moment to vomit at the scenes of cannibalism and art-wrought-from-the-neighbour's-flesh within.<br /> There's a few that MEATWAVE gets right into the intestines of, though. Some humans just click with the message so deeply that they see right through it and into the full code of the rite. It's enlightenment in a TV-screen-flash that lets them see the writhing guts of reality; revelation in the clamour of a thundering new music track that speaks more of the clatter of teeth and the crunch of gristle than whatever insipid lover the singer thinks they're spouting their emotions for. It's truth written in crimson light and sound.<br /> <br /> These humans suffer mental breakdowns, traumatic visions of a world of endless flesh unbroken by the barriers of self and skin, momentary glimpses of Twilight spirits and other nightmarish experiences in the aftermath of the MEATWAVE revelation. Those that don't break are the ones who, faced with the horrific truth, embrace it. They see that the world is a rash on the surface of a slithering hell-leviathan of gore and cartilage, and realise this knowledge is their opportunity. They're the ones that overcome their revulsion with a craving to discover more, or to use it for their own benefit. They see the endless meat and think it may just be the chance to indulge the appetites they've always held in check.<br /> <br /> MEATWAVE cultists forged in this way are remarkably capable of remaining outwardly calm and normal. Their brains seethe with spasmodic notions that slowly coalesce into a particular belief or dogma - that they can acquire occult power through cannibalism, or that they need to usher in a future where humanity is one unified flesh-organism to achieve its true potential, or that through blood and bone they can uplift themselves and others to a higher state. During a MEATWAVE outbreak, cultists in a given area naturally gravitate towards one another, able to sense other 'enlightened' ones; if this happens early enough, they will thrash out a mutual dogma as they struggle to understand what has happened to them. If it takes too long, the MEATWAVE cultists may end up in splintered factions, each believing that the others are heretics who are misinterpreting the holy message of meat, and begin waging a shadow war of brutal murder against each other.<br /> <br /> Once established, MEATWAVE cults try and carry through whichever divine message they believe is the truth. They monitor the airwaves for further holy writ, sometimes managing to track down the Claimed nodes at the heart of events. They try to acquire occult items of power or knowledge, attack other cults and occult groups, and craft their handiworks of flesh and blood. They give a name to the thing they worship - the Leviathan of Flesh, or the Lady of Hungers, or the Lord of Mount Pe'or, or the Thousand Crimson Letters, or other ostentatious titles. They try and invoke it, or spirits that serve it. They wait, though they do not know it, for the true architects of MEATWAVE - the Gluttons.<br /> <br /> To Uratha and other Essence-using beings, the cultists are mouth-wateringly alluring. They are like vessels that fleshy resonance collects in, their meat succulent with raw Essence. Devouring a cultist is a hit, a high, an orgasmic experience that demands repetition. Cultists are Essence pinatas unaware of the targets drawn on their souls.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Meat Cultist</b></span><br /> Int 3 Wits 2 Res 3 Str 3 Dex 2 Sta 3 Pre 2 Man 3 Com 3<br /> Academics 1 Investigation 2 Medicine 2 Occult 2 Athletics 2 Brawl 2 Drive 1 Firearms 1 Larceny 2 Weaponry 3 Empathy 1 Intimidate 2 Persuasion 2 Streetwise 1 Subterfuge 2<br /> <b>Merits: </b>Allies 2 (Varies), Contacts 2 (Varies), Iron Stamina 1, Resources 2<br /> Willpower 6 Health 8 Initiative 5 Defence 4 Speed 10<br /> <b>Addictive Essence:</b> A meat cultist gives twice the usual Essence to any werewolf devouring their flesh, and inflicts the Addicted Condition on the werewolf in the process.<br /> <b>Blood Rites:</b> A meat cultist is capable of performing and participating in the Shadowcall pack rite, but a meat-cultist-led Shadowcall rite requires the sacrifice of health levels equal to the spirit's Rank, either through bloodletting or flesh consumption. A meat cultist can learn additional pack rites, and can also acquire other supernatural merits once they reach Occult 3.<br /> <b>Flesh Is No Barrier: </b>A meat cultist can spend a Willpower point when making a Brawl or Weaponry attack to inflict the Arm Wrack, Leg Wrack or Blinded Tilts with the attack if it deals any lethal damage, or to grant it Armour Piercing 3.<br /> <b>Gristle Gnaw:</b> A meat cultist regains 1 health level for every four points of lethal damage inflicted on a human or human corpse by eating them. By eating the flesh of a human, a meat cultist gains some knowledge of the human's memories in the past month - it's mostly a hazy mess, but by spending a Willpower point, the cultist can fish out specifics or hunt for a particular bit of information they desire.<br /> <b>Unity Of Meat:</b> This capacity is not initially available, requiring at least one cultist in a group to reach Occult 4 before it becomes available. By touching another cultist, a cultist can spend 1 Willpower point and partially meld with them. This does not kill either cultist but is a ghastly fusion of cartilage and blood; the experience is ecstatic for all cultists involved. Initially the fusion is essentially just incapacitating, but as more cultists add themselves to the unity, its power grows. Every three cultists adds +1 to a Mental attribute of the gestalt horror, and grants it a minor Dread Power. The gestalt still needs to eat, and is likely entirely immobile; it can manifest mouths on any of its extremities for this purpose. Once sufficiently massive at 21 cultists or more, the gestalt can form new limbs that will allow it to move or attack, requiring a custom stat block depending on how it has evolved.<br /> <br /> Flesh cultists are, in some ways, the lucky ones. The ones who see the full revelation and break suffer a rather more extreme and immediate collapse. A MEATWAVE overload varies in how it manifests. Some victims literally fall apart, their body peeling away in layers to leave a bubbling, steaming pool of meat-petals and viscera that starts to spread tendrils and roots like some ghastly rendition of a plant. Some are driven to tap themselves directly into the holy message; forcing their heads or bodies against a television or antennae until their warped souls lead to a communion of meat and metal; a man lies, slumped, everything from the neck up nothing more than a tangle of meat meshed through the innards of a radio, vegetative and somehow not dead. Some turn inside-out in a moment of fleshy metamorphosis. Some vomit and vomit and vomit until it's just blood and guts, spin the mess into a hardening cocoon, and break out as ghastly Claimed where the spirit has literally been formed at the moment of the infection. Some have their insides liquefy and pour out, leaving them as moaning, slithering skin-things that roll along the floor looking for victims whose skin they can usurp. Sometimes more than one infectee occurs in the vicinity of another and they unify, little fragments of an imagined world without barriers between people - reduced to whining, oozing collectives of flesh that soon wither and die unless some sort of critical mass can be reached.<br /> <br /> Those are the side-effects, the detritus and cast-offs.<br /> <br /> Behind every outbreak there's an architect, a ritemaster who initiated the MEATWAVE. Gibbering Claimed and screaming cultists call them the Gluttons, these werewolves who have inflicted MEATWAVE on the world. Most Gluttons wait til the dying echoes of the infection have run their course, emerging to harvest the cults that have sprung up. They come, then, appearing to the cults as messengers or commanders, coralling them together and exploiting them. Sometimes a Glutton invokes the MEATWAVE rite for raw resources, eating cultists or using them as useful Claimed-Hosts or rendering their malleable flesh down for major-scale craftings of monstrous horrors or machinery of guts and teeth. Another Glutton may use the generated cults as pawns or minions, a quick-spawned powerbase; or perhaps as lures for other werewolves, dangling the cultists out to draw Uratha into tangling with them and becoming addicted to their flesh. Some Gluttons just want to cause chaos. A few believe in a twisted vision of the future, of humanity united via visceral, physical connections, and thus MEATWAVE is, to them, actual revelatory truth - they are missionaries of meat and maw. Lesser Gluttons don't have any grand plan or intent to exploit the outcome or other self-driven motivation, but are just carrying out the commands of their own master without any real interest in the overall purpose or possibilities.<br /> <br /> Who is the master? Who is it that MEATWAVE oozes forth from, with whom ancient pacts are the wellspring for the rite itself? Uratha point at the Gluttons and say<i> Bale Hound</i>. They say <i>Maeljin</i>. They say <i>Baalphegor</i>. But are they right? Is every Glutton really a servant of the Lord of Hunger - or are there just enough such Bale Hounds, naturally drawn to power like this, so as to make the Forsaken assume the deeper link where none such exists? Is this really Baalphegor's dreams of a future world, or is the Leviathan of Meat something else entirely? Are the nightmarish servants of Ten Thousand Crimson Words the perpetrators, or just another group that have taken advantage of the meat-dreams of some ghastly, hidden horror? And how on Earth did such a gristle nightmare become bound up with the reach and grasp of modern technology?<br /> <br /> MEATWAVE has its own, unexpected offshoots as well. There's the Flesh Collective, a unity of meat that has reached such levels of intellect that it desires transcendence from the mere physical; or the fungus-like colony of flesh that oozes through the pipes and basements of a major city and sprouts spirit-spores that Claim whatever they can bury themselves in; or the die-hard vegan movement that conceals a bizarre cult wanting to 'uplift' humanity into plant-Claimed, or the traveller-occultists who are constantly on the move, visiting new cultures and eating victims there to gain a greater understanding of the totality of human culture.<br /> <br /> Whatever the truth behind MEATWAVE, its grinning executives of spirit-flesh and meat-interwoven-with-metal, its gibbering cultists thrashing in orgasmic unity, its leering and hungry werewolves, those Forsaken who come across its outbreaks consider it a significant threat. It doesn't affect Uratha directly, but such a spiritual malaise that breaks down the constancy of flesh cannot be ignored. It's a reminder that the world as it is, is a fragile status-quo, easily disrupted by the shivers and twitches of whatever flesh-thing slithers and groans behind the walls of reality.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T08:14:04-08:00","id":1178794,"title":"","content":"Great as always. Loving the little easter eggs in the possible origins. I really want to either play or introduce as an npc one of those traveler occultits that want to &quot;have a taste&quot; of every human culture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T08:21:29-08:00","id":1178804,"title":"","content":"Well, MEATWAVE is terrifying. Its emphasis on flesh and breaking the status que is so against the God Machine's agenda that it hurts, and the fact that it melds flesh and technology is just a spit in the eye of the clockwork God. I'm totally gonna steal it for one of my anti God Machine antagonists (I call it the &quot;Living Devil&quot;, an ancient failed experiment of the God Machine which has exactly the same agenda presented in MEATWAVE- unity of flesh and challenging the status que).<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the use of the &quot;Ten Thousands Crimson Letters/Words&quot; and emphasis on cannibalism, freedom and occult knowledge falls right in the Prince of 100000 Leaves's alley (its cult is called the Red Word after all). Anyway, MEATWAVE feels like a much more interesting adaption of the Hunger from Antagonists. So many plot hooks, so much potential. Good work <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T10:25:42-08:00","id":1178856,"title":"","content":"Nice. I especially like the addiction and all around good-tastingness cultists offer for werewolves, and werewolves acting as sponsors and leaders of some of the cults.<br /> <br /> The other factions are interesting ideas as well, it's easy to see such a thing spawn into a lot of oddities like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T12:18:17-08:00","id":1178894,"title":"","content":"ALL HAIL THE NEW FLESH.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/40-dspaul","name":"DSPaul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T13:15:14-08:00","id":1178913,"title":"","content":"How deliciously terrifying","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T14:00:16-08:00","id":1178928,"title":"","content":"Freaking Lord of high heaven, that was the most horrifyingly fascinate and fascinatingly horrifying thing I\u2019ve read in ages. I recently bought a book where urban legends and spooky stories are collected, but now I fear that the book won\u2019t be so scary, between MEATWAVE and the Maiden of the Maw.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T15:11:31-08:00","id":1178962,"title":"","content":"This reminds of Bogleech's Parliament of the Old Flesh, but somehow at the same time less powerful and far scarier","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T17:54:14-08:00","id":1179028,"title":"","content":"While MEATWAVE doesn't get the primal disgust from me that the Maiden of the Maw did, I like it just the same. Keep up the good work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T10:03:29-08:00","id":1179240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1176040-five-pounds-of-meat?p=1178794#post1178794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great as always. Loving the little easter eggs in the possible origins. I really want to either play or introduce as an npc one of those traveler occultits that want to &quot;have a taste&quot; of every human culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the sort of minor weirdness I'm quite fond of, yeah.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1176040-five-pounds-of-meat?p=1178804#post1178804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the other hand, the use of the &quot;Ten Thousands Crimson Letters/Words&quot; and emphasis on cannibalism, freedom and occult knowledge falls right in the Prince of 100000 Leaves's alley (its cult is called the Red Word after all). Anyway, MEATWAVE feels like a much more interesting adaption of the Hunger from Antagonists. So many plot hooks, so much potential. Good work <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe originator of this particular entry was something that turned up in a 1e Forsaken chronicle I ran years ago; in that particular case, it was a crossover between the Prince of Ten Thousand Leaves and Baalphegorite Bale Hounds piggybacking onto something far deeper, complete with Disturbingly Tasty Cannibal Cultists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T11:01:46-08:00","id":1179258,"title":"","content":"My wife loves the idea of werewolves starting cults to feed their addiction for yummy peoplemeat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T11:07:13-08:00","id":1179259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1176040-five-pounds-of-meat?p=1179258#post1179258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My wife loves the idea of werewolves starting cults to feed their addiction for yummy peoplemeat.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't have just one!<br /> <br /> Also:<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm on a Vegan Diet.&quot;<br /> &quot;You are a Werewolf.&quot;<br /> &quot;Yes, I only eat Vegans.&quot;<br /> <br /> The true power behind MEATWAVE:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://smg.photobucket.com/user/jkscorch/media/meatwad_08.jpg.html\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><img src=\"http://smg.photobucket.com/user/jkscorch/media/meatwad_08.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><img src=\"http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v12/jkscorch/meatwad_08.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 01-25-2018, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T19:51:03-08:00","id":1179410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZP7K9SycELA\" data-code=\"ZP7K9SycELA\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/ZP7K9SycELA/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T14:07:11-08:00","id":1179605,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>The Perspective</b></span><br /> You dream. You rise from your bed, and open the curtains to reveal the moon, massive and bright - but it's not the moon at all, no, but instead a vast eye, glistening and staring. And this mad-eyed orb is no distant shape but there, <i>there</i>, right in front of you, pressed against the window, its discoloured and all-encompassing width blocking out all else but the bloodshot veins, the slithering worms that slide underneath its surface, the inky blackness at its centre.<br /> <br /> It stares at <i>you</i>, and you wake.<br /> <br /> You stagger to the bathroom, bleary-eyed, and groggily glance at the mirror. There's something wrong. You look closer; your eyes are bloodshot and yellowed from fatigue and ill health, the rigours of the long hours you work. There's movement. You look closer; the gaze of one of your eyes blurs. In the mirror, you see it: the pupil pulls apart, like liquid parting into two; the iris squirms as it splits to follow each budding centre. Pressure surges in your eye-socket, accompanied by pain; the eye pulls itself apart, a budding fission that completes with a ghastly noise. Two eyes now dwell in the socket; one of them is not yours. You start to panic. The eyes start to weep thick, greasy tears.<br /> <br /> They say knowledge is power, and this can be true; the times when it is most true are the times when it is most dangerous. Knowledge is not simply an ephemeral concept; it is imprinted in the world through the sparking neurones, sloshing chemicals and shivering energy fields of the human brain, both its meat anchor and whatever strange matrices it projects along unseen dimensions. Insert the right knowledge into that organic machinery and the combination of symbols and impulses turns it from a simple recollection into something powerful - a rite in miniature, an occult engine spasming frequencies that change the world. Some say this is how psychic powers manifest, but in the case of the Perspective, its how something utterly awful sinks its hooks into material existence.<br /> <br /> The Perspective manifests in human victims under specific circumstances. The first of these is that the human must have the Perspective Equation in their mind. Some humans deliberately seek the Equation out, or stumble upon it in the midst of advanced scientific theories; some accidentally create it by chaining together perfectly mundane thoughts and ideas into its shape. Once a Perspective outbreak is active, its manifestations may also force the Equation upon more victims. The second circumstance is that there must be an additional power source that gives the Equation a kickstart - usually this occurs in the form of unusually high levels of radioactivity in the subject. The above two conditions are usually met when a victim is exposed to a radioactive leak such as Fukushima or Chernobyl, or they work in a high-radioactivity environment, or are exposed to it for medical purposes. Occasionally, accidental exposure occurs through natural radioactive materials in mines and the like.<br /> <br /> A human possessing the Equation and exposed to radioactivity does not always result in an infection, though, indicating there is a third circumstance - the active attention of the Perspective itself. The Perspective appears capable of exerting will, indicating there is some actual level of intelligence behind the phenomenon, and it seems likely that it either chooses not to affect some potential victims, or simply isn't paying attention to every potential host.<br /> <br /> And so the genius theoretical physicist comes home after a day spent working on ground-breaking calculations and being doused in ever-so-slightly higher levels of particle radiation from the complex machinery in the labs; or the mining engineer emerges, gasping, from the deep uranium bore-passage and whimpers of the great, staring eye that blistered out of the rock and looked upon them; or the lonely patient sits at home, sick from the cures that have scoured their body with energies, and weeps. And the Perspective reaches out from its strange membrane of existence, and offers them a new view on things.<br /> <br /> It starts in the jelly of the eye. Infections spring up, leaving the orb hardened or weeping angry pus or like the pressure within will build up til it pops. Something changes in one of the eyes; it no longer obeys its owner, or it buds off siblings until the socket is utterly packed with squirming spheres or the bone around it cracks. Where weeping tracks of sour tears fall on flesh, a rash breaks out; blisters bubble and pop to reveal new eyes rising up. Where the tears fall on something other than the victim, they <i>still </i>bubble and seethe and burst into fleshy growth, leaving madly-swivelling eyes embedded in the floor or furniture or threading their fleshy roots through a hapless pet's flank. The Perspective cannot touch someone who actually has no eyes, but merely being blind is not enough to protect from its presence.<br /> <br /> The new eyes slither and squirm. They weep and spread their cancerous presence across the body. When too many share a nest, some burst forth to break and spatter on the ground. Some harden into polyps, erupting as coraline growths that grant even more eyeballs a perch. Some twist and reform so that their pupils are toothed openings, or so that long tongues lick and lap out of their centres. Where the victim's flesh is cut, the meat within bursts into fresh eyeballs. Scuttling spheres dart out of one opening, carried on glistening legs, and disappear into another. The victim vomits; a fat eyeballs slurps up out of their gullet and hits the floor, bursting apart into other, smaller eyes that root into the concrete. Some of the eyes are not even slightly human.<br /> <br /> The victim can see out of these new eyes, bestowed with a confusing and chaotic mess of vision. There's little they can do, though, because the eyes soon hijack the body utterly. The victim is not dead - they remain conscious and aware for as long as the damage done by the eyeball outbreak doesn't actually destroy the fundamental meat-mechanisms of their sentience - but they are locked out of their own flesh by the parliament of eyes that now controls their limbs, their lungs, their actions. The nightmare is compounded because the horrific visions of all the colony of spheres still pumps right into their brain. They can't shut it off or shut it down. The Perspective forces itself into existence through their witnessing.<br /> <br /> A hijacked Perspective host possesses some intelligence combined with a drive to change the local conditions of the world in which it has rooted itself. It needs to sustain its victim and refrain from actually killing them with the infestation - without their awareness, the Perspective would lose its anchor. It also has no particular drive to 'reproduce' - the Perspective does not feel a need to render more victims just for the sake of it, but will do so tactically for specific goals. This is simple enough - seize a human, keep them in place long enough to weep upon them or vomit a steaming spray of ocular matter on their flesh, then wait for the few hours that new Perspective eyeballs will take to bud on the infected. It's better to keep the new Perspective-infected subdued, as many will try to take their own lives once they figure out what is going on.<br /> <br /> With these new Perspective vessels, the originator will usually attempt to infect them on areas other than their face. The infection will cause their eyes to change and weep regardless, but if this can be controlled, it means the growing brood of vessels will have some of their own who can at least vaguely pass for human without covering their faces. These intermediaries can then serve to lure in new victims, acquire supplies, scout, or perform other functions for the eye-hive.<br /> <br /> Eyeballs that grow in non-human substrate still give their vision to the Perspective that created them, meaning that a Perspective-infested location may have eyes budding out of all manner of places in order to give an early-warning alarm system to the hive. These eyes will eventually die, however, unless they are embedded in a living being. Developed hosts gain the ability to retch up a fine-tuned concoction of Essence and organic matter that will provide nutrition to alarm-eyes that are not attached to living beings and that improve the connection between eye and vessel; an area that has been serving a hive as a lair for a while will have large swathes coated in the hardened muck of this vomit's residue.<br /> <br /> Once five or six vessels exist in a location, they will begin to network together, sharing their vision with each other - and the human consciousnesses that are serving as the data-hubs for their parliament of eyes. This involves a grotesque orgy of retched-up eyeballs and slime, slithering contact of flesh-on-flesh, and the consumption of some of each others' eyes, which needs to be repeated from time to time to keep the connection fresh. If the hive grows large enough, a single vessel is nominated as a 'pylon' and will mutate further into a shambling hulk of bulging brain matter, flesh-cords studded with eyeballs, and exchange-glands that allow it to plug into other vessels and reaffirm their connection with the hive's totality. Such pylons are the warped imprints of the Perspective's presence into the world.<br /> <br /> The presence of a hive would be bad enough, but this flesh-warping contamination is merely a method of facilitating what the Perspective is really after. As noted before, it doesn't reproduce for the sake of it. Past a certain point, additional victims are not infected fully but simply reanimated as husks, or eaten for sustenance, and ideally the hive will avoid any outside contact at all while it sets about its true purpose, although it may try and send out intermediaries to acquire radioactive materials or food. Someone stumbling upon a hive without being detected - an unlikely event, admittedly - will witness the utterly bizarre scene of the twisted, eye-peppered hosts engaged in strange, writhing dance or standing stock-still in staring meditation.<br /> <br /> In an of itself, this seems to do nothing. However, over time, the sheer eldritch power behind the Perspective's gaze saturates the local area through the medium of the eye-vessels' contemplation. Everything seems to grow a little lighter, a little better illuminated, a little airier; then, as the effect intensifies, the Gauntlet itself becomes transparent. In a strange fusion, both Flesh and Shadow become capable of seeing the other side as if through a glass pane; it's not a constant overlay, but rather from any given viewpoint a portion of the other side can be seen in the lines and angles of the world. Light crosses over; a fire in the Shadow will cast its illumination in the Flesh as well. Sunlight and moonlight illuminates just as starkly. The transparency is visible to all, including mortals. Perspective-Infected will often collect mirrors and other reflective surfaces, decorating their lair and area of influence with as many things that collect and reflect the light as possible.<br /> <br /> This transparency slowly spreads, usually covering no more than a few dozen yards from the hive's heart. The sense of airy light spreads further - hundreds of yards, even a mile, wherein everything seems brighter, although curiously not more colourful. If anything, the brighter illumination actually gives more of a sense of glaring or washed-out contrast. The larger the eye-hive, the larger each effect, but once a hive has established itself, the Perspective does not seem massively interested in expanding its domain. It simply tries to retain its control over the infected area, and to fend off interlopers who would purge its influence.<br /> <br /> In unusual circumstances where an infection manages to last a year or more, a further transformation falls upon the infected area. Any pylon that is present will absorb two or three more hosts into its biomass, turn sessile, and begin to stretch its fleshy, eye-studded tendrils into the shape of a bounded opening. The portal itself does not seem to lead anywhere, but a new membrane of reality becomes visible in the angles and the distances of the infected region - not the Shadow or Flesh, but instead glimpses of some other place. This third layer seems empty, but bright; it calls to mind a deserted structure, spartan and bare, all light-bleached stone and stark edges. Things can be spotted there - brief, flitting shapes that soon hurry round the corner of nowhere. Sometimes, the view is blocked by a vast, ichorous eye, unblinking and wide. Sometimes that eye appears in the bounded portal of the pylon. When it does, it weeps corrosive tears through into the world. Vessels come to lick and lap at the oozing muck as if it were the most delightful ambrosia.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Perspective-Infected</b></span><br /> Int 3 Wits 8 Res 3 Str 3 Dex 5 Sta 3 Pre 3 Man 2 Com 3<br /> Investigation 5 Medicine 1 Occult 3 Athletics 4 Brawl 3 Stealth 4 Survival 3 Weaponry 1 Empathy 2 Intimidation 3 Subterfuge 2<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Iron Stamina 1<br /> Willpower 6 Essence 8 Health 8 Initiative 8 Defence 9 Speed 13<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Blinding Spray 3, Eye Spy, Gauntlet Cloak, Hunter's Senses (Everything), Reality Stutter, Venomous Ichor<br /> <b>Eye Infection:</b> A Perspective-Infected that succeeds in a grapple can, instead of one of the normal moves, spend 1 Essence to attempt to infect a target. The victim must succeed at a Stamina + Resolve roll with a -5 penalty, or gains the moderate Sick Tilt. If a mortal human being, the victim is also now infected with the Perspective; eyes will begin to burst from their flesh and tears over the coming hours. Werewolves also suffer from eyes budding out of their skin, but the infection quickly burns itself out and the invading orbs are consumed by the regenerating meat.<br /> <b>Contemplation:</b> Every hour that a Perspective-Infected spends simply observing the surrounding area, uninterrupted, restores a single point of Essence.<br /> <b>Parliament of Eyes:</b> A Perspective-Infected does not need to spend 1 Essence per hour to maintain its Eye Spy Dread Power.<br /> <b>Warped Perspective: </b>By spending 1 Essence, a Perspective-Infected may reflexively observe the world and alter reality for a round based on the perspective of its own vision. Any of the following effects can be selected, as long as the target is not in an area of complete or near darkness.<ul><li>It can add reduce the Speed of a target by 8; the prey actually moves at its normal speed, but the distance it needs to travel seems to stretch and lengthen out.</li> <li>The Infected can make a Brawl attack against a target it can see, adding +1 Strength for every full 10 yards away the victim is, to a maximum of +8 at 80 yards or more.</li> <li>The Infected can redefine 'down' for both themselves and a single target for the round; they are affected as if gravity were pulling in a different direction to normal.</li> <li>The Infected can interact with anyone it can see in a mirror as if they were actually present in front of the mirror, including attacking them. This effect does not extend to other forms of projected image such as a TV screen.</li> <li>The Infected can deny a target the bonus to perception checks from Observe Gauntlet, and instead levy it as a penalty to perception checks instead.</li> </ul><b>Corpse Puppet:</b> A Perspective-Infected can touch a living human being who is unconscious or incapacitated and spend 1 Essence to transfer a single eyeball from the Infected to the prey; the eyeball squirms in through an orifice or wound and seizes control of the victim's body. The victim is now puppetted - not a true Infected, but effectively a zombie under the Infected's control. The Infected can empathetically grant the zombie instructions via touch or line of sight. While the zombie is initially 'alive' it will fight on to its complete incapacitation; even if the host is killed, the body needs to be fully boxed out with aggravated damage, or the resident eyeball found and killed. Even decapitation may not necessarily stop the puppet.<br /> <b>Radioactive Regeneration:</b> Every hour a Perspective-Infected spends in an area with unusually high levels of radiation, it regenerates a single point of lethal or aggravated damage. Perspective-Infected do not suffer damage from high radiation levels.<br /> <b>Observe Gauntlet:</b> With each hour of constant work, costing 1 Essence in the process, a Perspective-Infected can observe the Gauntlet to render the barrier between worlds transparent, adding a +1 bonus to Perception checks on either side of the Gauntlet to a maximum of +5. This affects an area of 10 square yards. This also causes a constant level of at least low illumination on either side, regardless of how dark it should be. After a month of observation, the Gauntlet then becomes truly transparent, allowing creatures on either side to see the other world without meaningful obstacle.<br /> <b>Sour Light: </b>After being present in an area for a year where the Gauntlet has been rendered transparent, a hive of Perspective-Infected gain new abilities. The first of these is that they can spend 5 Essence and pass through a pylon portal to emerge through any door or aperture within a ten mile radius that is currently illuminated; this cost reduces to 1 Essence if the target is lit up by natural sunlight. Areas that are in deep shadow or total dark are utterly inaccessible via this transport. The second ability is that any Perspective-Infected in the hive can spend 1 Essence and force any target they can see to pass a Stamina + Resolve check or suffer the moderate Sick Tilt. After an hour, the target's infection increases to the Blind Tilt. If five or more Perspective-Infected come together and spend 5 Essence each at the pylon, they can indiscriminately inflict this effect randomly across all targets within ten miles - a horrible outbreak of ocular infections - or can turn the pylon portal to the purpose of scrying, looking at any illuminated locations within ten miles. They can then attempt to infect a single target seen through the pylin with the above effect, but with the grave Sick Tilt rather than merely moderate, and with the Blind Tilt taking effect after three rounds.<br /> <br /> It's not surprising that there are Hunters in Darkness who believe the Perspective to be a Host. They infect people and mutilate the Gauntlet. Yet there are a number of clear characteristics that do not match up to those of known Hosts such as the Rat and Spider. The Perspective do not take the form of warped animals, they do not have discrete 'Shards' that attempt to escape from a Host body if it is destroyed, they can add to their numbers via infection with relative ease, and they do not dwell within the world - Perspective infections occur only under unusual circumstances, and seem to exude from some other place entirely. A few loremasters have posited that the Perspective actually dwells within the Gauntlet, somehow sealed off until conditions are right for it to break out and establish a 'lens' through Perspective-Infected. No legend speaks of Wolf doing battle with some sort of 'Eye-Demon', though, and most werewolves dismiss the notion of some giant evil eyeball in the times of Pangaea as being patently absurd.<br /> <br /> That said, a few <i>Menina </i>believe that, yes, the Perspective has unusual characteristics due to whatever prison or hidden membrane of reality it may dwell in, but that it is not so alien as it may initially seen. There are hints in dreams, carefully filtered from those of Cahalith and sensitive mortals, and a few unreliable snatches of things seen in that strange other place - including brief moments before that great eye comes staring out, when what surrounds the orb might be glimpsed for half a breath. Those dreams and sights speak of something just as ghastly and warped as that sick eye, but of an avian aspect. Such Hunters in Darkness, then, posit that however it ended up where it is, however it ended up so diseased that its presence in the world is that of contagious, maddening eyes rather than its own true form, that this really is some beast-god of the ancient days; a caged bird, indeed.<br /> <br /> To others, the answer is less dogmatic. Not every Host need be a relic of that glorious age, nor follow the same paradigm as the Beshilu and Azlu. This may be something else that simply matches the same pattern, but from different origins. A few Uratha wonder if the Perspective is in fact <b><i>the </i></b>observer - a being that witnesses everything and, through witnessing everything, renders everything real. This take on the Perspective has it that the eye is in fact entirely 'natural' to the world, but that clearly it is sick and ill - that something has crawled from the darkness and nestled in cysts and blisters, that the Perspective is a victim here and the infected not its handiwork but simply its tears. Perhaps the Perspective can be cured or scoured clean. Then there are those who look upon it and say, <i>this is not a creature of our world</i>. They point to the gateways of the pylons, and the glimpses of a strange and empty, bright place beyond, and believe the Infected are some sort of biomechanical system designed to open paths from some sort of hub-realm, a place that has been rendered empty by extinction or collapse but to which the servitor-gates continue to operate. What desolate lands might be found beyond where the eye stares, if one could but find a way of fully opening a pylon gateway and stepping through? Few Uratha have contemplated what the nature of the Perspective Equation may mean, though - what the signal found in particular patterns of the mind itself might indicate about the Perspective's nature.<br /> <br /> With depressing inevitability, there are those humans to whom the ghastly, unreasoning nature of a Perspective outbreak is not a source of horror but of gleeful opportunism. Indeed, some occultists have been known to purposefully coax an outbreak into existence, sacrificing victims who have been forced to learn the Perspective Equation and exposed to radioactive materials. These occultists see a giant, staring eye beyond the walls of reality as a god worthy of worship or an energy source to be parasitically drained; they offer up victims to a growing hive in return for some measure of interaction, or they draw upon its power with their own prepared rites.<br /> <br /> Unsurprisingly, most occultists trying to exploit or worship the Perspective end up victims of it, their groaning bodies overrun by a plague of eyes that force them to witness every monstrous day in all-encompassing vision. A few, though, are sufficiently well-girded with sorcerous rites or just plain lucky enough to pull it off. These warlocks acquire and contain the Perspective's power for their own, or at least a measure thereof, transforming themselves into monstrosities in return for the ability to make the world itself reflect how they see it.<br /> <br /> A few other human interactions with the Perspective have been recorded in the past. Some organisations have attempted to combat, analyse or harvest it; there is at least one rogue blacker-than-black government agency trying to use the Perspective as a source of remote-viewing powers on test subjects, and a corporation that has figured out how to refine a serum from the reality-warping illness that augments perception at the cost of sanity. Where the Perspective is allowed to exist and fester for a while, those alienated groups and individuals forced to deal with the reality of the infection can fall into cultic or survivalist behaviour, including gouging their own eyes out to prevent the infection from taking root in them in the first place. A few brave souls try to map Perspective outbreaks in the hope of figuring out just what the eye they saw in their dreams is actually trying to witness in the world. An old Kazakhstani woman, her body wracked by the cancers of a youth spent in the uranium mines, fervently turns her charisma and resources to gathering uranium for her own ends. She seeks union with that vast, staring eye that has seethed in her thoughts for over half a century - a union to be sealed with the blazing fire of a nuclear detonation, her wedding gift for and vengeance upon the watcher beyond.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Eyeccultist</b></span><br /> Int 4 Wits 7 Res 4 Str 3 Dex 4 Sta 4 Pre 5 Man 3 Com 4<br /> Academics 3 Investigation 4 Medicine 2 Occult 4 Athletics 2 Brawl 2 Firearms 4 Weaponry 2 Empathy 4 Intimidation 2 Persuasion 2 Subterfuge 3<br /> <b>Merits: </b>Allies 2 (Varies), Contacts 2 (Varies), Trained Observer 2, Resources 3<br /> Willpower 8 Essence 10 Health 9 Initiative 8 Defence 6 Speed 12<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Eye Spy, Reality Stutter<br /> <b>Consume Eyes:</b> An eyeccultist regains 5 points of Essence by consuming the eyes of a living or freshly dead human being, and gains access to the victim's visual memories from the past week.<br /> <b>Total Perspective:</b> By spending 1 Essence, an eyeccultist may reflexively observe the world and alter reality for a round based on the perspective of its own vision. Any of the following effects can be selected, as long as the target is not in an area of complete or near darkness.<ul><li>It can add reduce the Speed of a target by 7; the prey actually moves at its normal speed, but the distance it needs to travel seems to stretch and lengthen out.</li> <li>It can increase its own Speed by 7; again, it moves no faster, but strangely the distance it covers just seems to be shorter.</li> <li>The eyeccultist can make a Brawl attack against a target it can see, adding +1 Strength for every full 10 yards away the victim is, to a maximum of +7 at 70 yards or more.</li> <li>The eyeccultist can interact with anyone it can see in a mirror as if they were actually present in front of the mirror, including attacking them. This effect does not extend to other forms of projected image such as a TV screen.</li> <li>The eyeccultist can perceive any point it can see from any angle, regardless of the actual angle between eyeccultist and point. This allows it to see round corners, see the face of someone who has their back to it, etc.</li> <li>The eyeccultist can make perception and Investigation rolls against the entire area it can perceive, easily sifting through all the visual information regardless of the sheer amount it may need to process; it can identify the number of people wearing green scarves out of a crowd of thousands in a few seconds, for example.</li> <li>The eyeccultist can see clearly across the Gauntlet, or across any other occult barrier that it is aware of.</li> </ul><b>Eyeruption: </b>The eyeccultist can spend 1 Essence to remove the Blind Tilt by sprouting new eyes on any part of its body; these eyes remain for up to an hour before submerging once more. If the eyeccultist touches another living being, it can use its Eye Spy Dread Power to actually embed an eye in the target for the Power's duration.<br /> <b>Sore Weeping:</b> The eyeccultist can spend 1 Essence and force a target it can see to make a Stamina + Resolve roll; failure means the target gains the moderate Sick Tilt, and gains the Blind Tilt after three rounds.<br /> <b>Contained Perspective: </b>When the eyeccultist makes a dramatic failure on a roll in a scene where it has used a supernatural power, it must pass a Stamina + Resolve check or become a Perspective-Infected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175